{
  "id": "COMPOUND:802 - PROTEIN:1417",
  "verbalization": "Acetazolamide is implicated in the targeting of DNA gyrase subunit B through a series of intermediate targets, including Penicillin-binding protein 1A and Fuscaxanthone C. The evidence suggests that acetazolamide exerts its biological effect by interacting with Penicillin-binding protein 1A, which in turn targets DNA gyrase subunit B. This pathway implies a mechanism where acetazolamide may modulate the activity of Penicillin-binding protein 1A, potentially influencing DNA gyrase function. The shared involvement of Penicillin-binding protein 1A in both pathways underscores a possible common mechanism, though the exact nature of acetazolamide's interaction with this protein remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Penicillin-binding protein 1A as a critical mediator in the relationship between acetazolamide and DNA gyrase subunit B.",
